                <pb facs="0253" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9603: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-21T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 21—1:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1016. Following from commander in chief: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The landing party sent ashore from United States Ship <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Asheville</hi> at Yeungkong, Kwangtung, on 18th
                            November reported there had been small disturbance ashore and few shots
                            fired at Catholic mission but Presbyterian mission not attacked. All
                            Americans safe. Yangtze quiet.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
